# The browse service handler (node-local): given a request { path }, list
# that directory in this node's OWN read-only view and return the rows.
# `fs-rows` reads the local view — the view never crosses the fabric, only
# the rows value (a data list) does, riding the session-buffer transport
# back to the caller. Unwrap the result to a plain list (data), since a
# result value cannot cross.
match (fs-rows ($in | get "path")) {
  ok $r => $r
  _ => []
}
